---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Spiritual Companionship | Liberating Scripture Collective"
  description="A growing network of spiritual companions and directors whose practice is explicitly liberationist, trauma-informed, and radically inclusive. Consent-based accompaniment."
  canonical="https://liberatingscripture.org/spiritual-direction/"
  ogImage="https://liberatingscripture.org/assets/og/og-spiritual-direction.png"
  ogImageAlt="Spiritual companionship with the Liberating Scripture Collective"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script
      type="application/ld+json"
      is:inline
      set:html={JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@graph": [
          {
            "@type": "Service",
            "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/spiritual-direction/#service",
            name: "Spiritual Companionship",
            description:
              "A growing network of spiritual companions and directors whose practice is explicitly liberationist, trauma-informed, and radically inclusive.",
            url: "https://liberatingscripture.org/spiritual-direction/",
            serviceType: "Spiritual Companionship",
            provider: { "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/#organization" },
          },
          {
            "@type": "WebPage",
            "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/spiritual-direction/#webpage",
            url: "https://liberatingscripture.org/spiritual-direction/",
            name: "Spiritual Companionship | Liberating Scripture Collective",
            isPartOf: { "@id": "https://liberatingscripture.org/#website" },
          },
        ],
      })}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="sd-page">
    <header class="sd-hero">
      <div class="content">
        <p class="eyebrow">Accompaniment</p>
        <h1>Spiritual Companionship</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Consent-based, trauma-aware spiritual accompaniment, walking alongside
          people with presence, attentiveness, and care.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="sd-content content">
      <section class="sd-section" aria-labelledby="sd-what">
        <h2 id="sd-what">What is spiritual companionship?</h2>
        <p>
          Spiritual companionship is a practice of attentive presence, a shared
          listening for what is alive, stirring, or asking to be named in a
          person's life. It includes classical spiritual direction, and it makes
          room for other consent-based forms of accompaniment too. It makes space
          for prayer, reflection, silence, and honest exploration, trusting that
          God meets people as they are. At its heart, it is about listening for
          the Spirit together and joining in a posture of openness to Christ.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is not advice, correction, diagnosis, or spiritual performance. It
          is not about fixing faith, managing behavior, or submitting to an
          expert or authority figure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Within the Liberating Scripture Collective, spiritual companionship
          explicitly resists shame, coercion, and the use of religious language
          as a means of control. It honors agency, attends to the body and lived
          experience, and trusts that the Spirit's work unfolds over time
          through relationship, honesty, and consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="sd-section" aria-labelledby="sd-lsc">
        <h2 id="sd-lsc">Spiritual companionship and LSC</h2>
        <p>
          We are in the early stages of building a directory of spiritual
          companions and directors whose practice is explicitly liberationist, trauma-informed,
          and radically inclusive. These directors will not share a single
          method, style, or spiritual perspective, but they will share core
          commitments: to consent, to respect for boundaries, to restorative
          justice, and to an understanding of spiritual growth that does not
          require fear, shame, or erasure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="sd-section sd-questions" aria-labelledby="sd-for-whom">
        <h2 id="sd-for-whom">The directory</h2>
        <p>
          This future directory is being built for people asking questions like:
        </p>
        <ul class="sd-questions__list">
          <li>
            How do I remain open to God after religious harm or exhaustion?
          </li>
          <li>
            How do I discern what is life-giving without surrendering my agency?
          </li>
          <li>
            How do I pray or listen for the Spirit without reenacting old
            patterns of pressure or performance?
          </li>
          <li>
            How do I integrate faith, justice, healing, and honesty in a way
            that honors my body and story?
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          As this work develops, this space will host a curated list of
          spiritual directors whose practice aligns with the commitments of the
          LIT and the broader work of the Collective. Participation will not be
          based on credentials alone, but on demonstrated ethical clarity,
          theological transparency, and respect for the dignity and autonomy of
          those they accompany.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="sd-cta-grid">
        <div class="sd-cta-card">
          <h3>Are you a spiritual director?</h3>
          <p>
            If your work is rooted in liberation, inclusion, and trauma-aware
            care, you're welcome to reach out about joining the directory when
            it launches.
          </p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn"><span>Get in touch</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="sd-cta-card">
          <h3>Are you seeking accompaniment?</h3>
          <p>
            This space will evolve as the work takes shape. Just as spiritual
            direction is an experience of careful relationship, so too will this
            gathering of directors be built with care. Stay with us.
          </p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--outline"
            ><span>Stay in touch</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .sd-hero {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem) 0;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .sd-hero .content {
    max-width: calc(64 * var(--ch));
  }

  .sd-hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 5px;
    background: var(--green);
  }

  .sd-hero h1 {
    font-family: "Crimson Text", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.5vw, 3.8rem);
    color: var(--text-strong);
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .sd-hero .eyebrow {
    color: var(--green-text);
  }

  .sd-content {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  .sd-section {
    max-width: calc(64 * var(--ch));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .sd-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--green);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .sd-section p {
    max-width: calc(68 * var(--ch));
  }

  .sd-questions__list {
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .sd-questions__list li {
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .sd-cta-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .sd-cta-card {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 2rem;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .sd-cta-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .sd-cta-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .sd-cta-card .btn {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .sd-cta-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
